## Accessibility Target

**WCAG 2.2 Level AA** ← all components must meet this standard.

Key criteria to verify in PRs:

- SC 2.4.11 (Focus Not Obscured)
- SC 2.5.8 (Target Size / 24×24 pixels)
- SC 2.5.7 (Dragging Movements / keyboard alternative)
- SC 3.3.8 (Accessible Authentication / no paste-block)
- SC 3.3.7 (Redundant Entry / autocomplete support)
- SC 3.2.6 (Consistent Help / layout constancy)

---

## Do's and Don'ts

✅ **Do:**

- Consult `.ai/` knowledge base before any major work
- Use async fs from `_fs-utils.mjs`
- Keep error messages terse with prefix symbols (✔, ⚠, ❌, ▶, ℹ, ⏭)
- Verify native semantics (extend, don't replace)
- Test with real screen readers
- Design for keyboard-first access

❌ **Don't:**

- Use `tabindex > 0` (breaks tab order)
- Remove focus outline without replacement
- Communicate state by color alone
- Use role when native element exists
- Block paste on auth inputs
- Use `aria-hidden` on interactive elements
- Create targets smaller than 24×24 CSS pixels (SC 2.5.8)

